  "scope": "Five focused native process-loss cases pass. External SIGKILL is exercised after a command response, during an uncompleted command with a checkpointed host save, after a real remote push before its acknowledgement, before final command metadata publication and after durable publication before response delivery. Before publication, recovery keeps the prior acknowledged draft and interrupted marker; after publication it restores the completed draft whose response was lost. New JVMs preserve original commits, binary bytes, archive references, baselines and receipts, and recover uncertain remote writes with zero repeat pushes. Recovered drafts save successfully. All five cases, lease closure and fixture cleanup pass. Authentication is synthetic. The focused mode does not repeat the full native batch, prove power-loss durability or replace real-account and actual-client acceptance.",
